@WWSHA.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5159

### ===========================================================================
### Phase 4 smoke workflow
### Run the requests in order. Named requests feed IDs into later requests.
### ===========================================================================

### 0. Health
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Register three heroes with funny names and questionable powers.
###    Each returns 201 with availability = "Available" and reputation = 0.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1a. Hero A
# @name registerHeroA
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Captain Procrastination",
  "superpower": "Saves the day tomorrow"
}

### 1b. Hero B
# @name registerHeroB
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Incredible Sulk",
  "superpower": "Emotional damage at close range"
}

### 1c. Hero C
# @name registerHeroC
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mildly Inconvenienced Man",
  "superpower": "Files a strongly worded complaint"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. File incident A. A hero is available, so status = "InProgress",
###    assignmentId is set, and one hero is assigned.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2a. Incident A
# @name fileIncidentA
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city": "Townsville",
  "occurredAt": "2026-11-11T09:00:00",
  "description": "A villain stole every left shoe in town.",
  "category": "SupervillainAppearance"
}

### 2b. Confirm incident A is InProgress with one assigned hero
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. File incident B. A second available hero is assigned.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3a. Incident B
# @name fileIncidentB
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city": "Springfield",
  "occurredAt": "2026-11-11T10:00:00",
  "description": "A kaiju is politely waiting in line at the bakery.",
  "category": "WanderingKaiju"
}

### 3b. Confirm incident B is InProgress
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentB.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. File incident C. The third available hero is assigned.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4a. Incident C
# @name fileIncidentC
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city": "Shelbyville",
  "occurredAt": "2026-11-11T11:00:00",
  "description": "Two heroes argued about the correct way to save a cat.",
  "category": "DisagreementBetweenHeros"
}

### 4b. Confirm incident C is InProgress
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentC.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. File incident D. No hero is available, so it stays "Opened".
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a. Incident D
# @name fileIncidentD
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city": "Ogdenville",
  "occurredAt": "2026-11-11T12:00:00",
  "description": "An alien invasion is scheduled for next Tuesday.",
  "category": "AlienInvasion"
}

### 5b. Confirm incident D is Opened with no assignment
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. File two damage reports against incident D while it is Opened.
###    Both have assignmentId = null; damageReportCount = 2.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6a. Report D1
# @name fileReportD1
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "A mailbox was reduced to splinters.",
  "severity": "Moderate",
  "cost": 250,
  "injury": 0,
  "reportedAt": "2026-11-11T12:15:00"
}

### 6b. Report D2
# @name fileReportD2
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "The town fountain now glows an unsettling green.",
  "severity": "Severe",
  "cost": 1500,
  "injury": 1,
  "reportedAt": "2026-11-11T12:20:00"
}

### 6c. Confirm incident D still has two reports and no assignment
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. File one damage report against incident A (InProgress).
###    damageReportCount = 1 and the report joins the assignment history.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7a. Report A1
# @name fileReportA1
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "A parked car was mildly inconvenienced.",
  "severity": "Minor",
  "cost": 100,
  "injury": 0,
  "reportedAt": "2026-11-11T09:30:00"
}

### 7b. Confirm incident A has one report
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Close incident A.
###    One assessment: damageReportCount = 1, reputationDelta = 4.
###    The assigned hero's reputation becomes 4 and the hero is freed.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8a. Close incident A
# @name closeIncidentA
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}/close
Content-Type: application/json

### 8b. Confirm incident A is Closed
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. Check incident D.
###    The freed hero was auto-assigned to the oldest Opened incident (D),
###    so D is InProgress and both reports now have an assignmentId.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 9a. Incident D after auto-dispatch
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 9b. Incident D's assignment
# @name getIncidentDAssignment
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/assignment
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. Get the freed hero's detail and assessments.
###     Reputation is 4 and the assessment is present.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 10a. Hero A detail
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes/{{registerHeroA.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 10b. Hero A assessments
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes/{{registerHeroA.response.body.$.id}}/assessments
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. Attempt to assign the busy hero A to incident B.
###     Returns 409 with code "hero.unavailable".
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 11a. Busy hero rejection
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentB.response.body.$.id}}/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "heroId": "{{registerHeroA.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 12. Attempt to file a report against closed incident A.
###     Returns 409 with code "incident.closed".
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 12a. Closed incident rejection
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentA.response.body.$.id}}/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Too late, the paperwork is already filed.",
  "severity": "Minor",
  "cost": 1,
  "injury": 0
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 13. Register two more heroes and add both to incident D.
###     A third new hero is registered so the fourth-assignment rejection
###     can be exercised. All three remain Available.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 13a. Hero E
# @name registerHeroE
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Procrastinating Porcupine",
  "superpower": "Eventually gets around to it"
}

### 13b. Hero F
# @name registerHeroF
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Doctor Maybe",
  "superpower": "Answers every question with a shrug"
}

### 13c. Hero G (reserved for the assignment-full rejection)
# @name registerHeroG
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Unassignable",
  "superpower": "Arrives precisely one minute too late"
}

### 13d. Add hero E to incident D
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "heroId": "{{registerHeroE.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 13e. Add hero F to incident D
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "heroId": "{{registerHeroF.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 13f. Attempt to add a fourth hero to incident D
###      Returns 409 with code "assignment.full".
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/heroes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "heroId": "{{registerHeroG.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 13g. Confirm incident D has three assigned heroes
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 14. Close incident D.
###     Three assessments: damageReportCount = 2, reputationDelta = 3 each.
###     Hero A's reputation ends at 7.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 14a. Close incident D
# @name closeIncidentD
POST {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/{{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}/close
Content-Type: application/json

### 14b. Confirm hero A's final reputation
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes/{{registerHeroA.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 14c. All assessments for incident D
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/assessments?incidentId={{fileIncidentD.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 15. Query filters
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 15a. Opened incidents (none remain after the workflow)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?status=Opened
Accept: application/json

### 15b. InProgress incidents
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?status=InProgress
Accept: application/json

### 15c. Closed incidents (A and D)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?status=Closed
Accept: application/json

### 15d. Category filter
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?category=WanderingKaiju
Accept: application/json

### 15e. City filter
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?city=Ogdenville
Accept: application/json

### 15f. Invalid status filter (400)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents?status=NotAStatus
Accept: application/json

### 15g. Available heroes (A, E, and F were freed when D closed; G was never assigned)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes?available=true
Accept: application/json

### 15h. Unavailable heroes (B and C remain busy)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes?available=false
Accept: application/json

### 15i. Open assignments (incidents B and C remain InProgress)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/assignments?open=true
Accept: application/json

### 15j. All assignments
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/assignments
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 16. OpenAPI document
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 16a. OpenAPI v1
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### 16b. Missing hero (404)
GET {{WWSHA.Api_HostAddress}}/api/heroes/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json
